<style>
/* Layout: the RxC results template, in the Kooyong brand from moniqueryan.com.au: deep indigo #190d51 (the
   site's primary) for headings, solid buttons and dark surfaces, its bright teal #00b4ce for the boxed headline
   line and accents, and its pale teal for the hero; Outfit for headings and Open Sans for text, as on her site.
   The two group colours are gold and violet, as on every page. Her site's palette is indigo and lavender, the
   same hue as the violet used on other pages, so here Group 2's violet is warmer (#8a4fd0, about 17 degrees
   round from her indigo) and never sits on a lavender or indigo fill: both group cards share one neutral grey,
   and the page uses no lavender at all. No red marks a group or the change most voters opposed. */
:root{
  --indigo:#190d51; --teal:#00b4ce; --teal-dk:#318ba3; --teal-ink:#1f6f83; --mist:#ccf0f5; --foam:#eef9fb;
  --g1:#a97c0c; --g2:#8a4fd0; --gsoft:#f3f5f7;
  --paper:#ffffff; --ink:#1c1838; --heading:#190d51; --card:#ffffff; --muted:#585670;
  --line:rgba(28,24,56,.14); --track:#e3e7ea; --tint:#eef9fb; --deep:#190d51; --frame:rgba(28,24,56,.18);
  --sea:#0f3d48; --agree-bg:#ccf0f5; --agree-ink:#190d51; --agree-trk:rgba(25,13,81,.18);
  --display:"Outfit",system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Arial,sans-serif;
  --text:"Open Sans",system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Arial,sans-serif;
  color-scheme:light;
  box-sizing:border-box;
  padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);
  padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px);
}
/* Dark mode keeps the hero in the brand's light teal; elsewhere a dark teal-slate, not the MP's indigo, so the
   violet group never sits on an indigo ground. */
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
    --g1:#bb8b1a; --g2:#a77be6; --gsoft:#19333b;
    --paper:#0b1a1f; --ink:#e6f2f4; --heading:#e6f2f4; --card:#112830; --muted:#a5bcc1;
    --line:rgba(255,255,255,.15); --track:#24393f; --tint:#0e252b; --deep:#08161a; --frame:rgba(255,255,255,.16);
    --sea:#07171b; --agree-bg:#163f49; --agree-ink:#e6f2f4; --agree-trk:rgba(255,255,255,.22); color-scheme:dark;
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --g1:#bb8b1a; --g2:#a77be6; --gsoft:#19333b;
  --paper:#0b1a1f; --ink:#e6f2f4; --heading:#e6f2f4; --card:#112830; --muted:#a5bcc1;
  --line:rgba(255,255,255,.15); --track:#24393f; --tint:#0e252b; --deep:#08161a; --frame:rgba(255,255,255,.16);
    --sea:#07171b; --agree-bg:#163f49; --agree-ink:#e6f2f4; --agree-trk:rgba(255,255,255,.22); color-scheme:dark;
}
*,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:inherit}
html{scroll-padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);scroll-behavior:smooth;-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}
body{margin:0;font-family:var(--text);color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);font-size:18px;line-height:1.55;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
.wrap{max-width:77.5rem;margin:0 auto;padding:0 40px}
h1,h2,h3{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:var(--heading)}
p{margin:0}
a{color:inherit}
:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ink);outline-offset:3px}
.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:.72rem 1.25rem .74rem;border-radius:6px;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:1.06rem;letter-spacing:0;line-height:1.1;text-decoration:none;border:2px solid var(--indigo);cursor:pointer}
.btn.solid{background:var(--indigo);color:#fff}
.btn.line{background:transparent;color:var(--indigo)}
.btn:hover{transform:translateY(-1px)}
.dot{width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;display:inline-block;flex:none}
.dot.g1{background:var(--g1)} .dot.g2{background:var(--g2)}
.pill{display:inline-block;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:.92rem;line-height:1;background:var(--indigo);color:#fff;border-radius:4px;padding:.38rem .7rem .4rem}
q{quotes:"“" "”"}

/* ---------- hero ---------- */
.hero{background:var(--mist);color:var(--indigo);overflow:hidden}
.hero h1{color:var(--indigo)}
.hero :focus-visible{outline-color:var(--indigo)}
.hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr 1fr;gap:48px;align-items:center;padding:80px 0 92px}
/* The headline is three set lines, the middle one boxed in the brand's teal. Its longest line, box included,
   is 7.6em wide in Outfit Bold (measured in Chrome), so it is sized from its column and capped by the window height. */
.hero-text{container-type:inline-size;min-width:0}
.hero h1{font-size:min(12.6cqi,10vh,5.8rem);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-bottom:26px}
.hero h1 .ln{display:block;white-space:nowrap}
.hero h1 .box{display:inline-block;background:var(--teal);color:var(--indigo);padding:.02em .2em .08em;margin:.1em 0 .12em -.2em;border-radius:.08em}
.hero .sub{font-size:1.22rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:31rem;margin-bottom:32px;font-weight:600}
.hero .turnout{font-size:.95rem;font-weight:600;margin-top:22px}
.actions{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.cards{position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px;padding-top:max(10px,calc(3.43rem - 56px))}
/* the sticker is the brand's indigo, its figure in the brand's teal (6.9:1) and its words in white */
.sticker{position:relative;width:8.25rem;height:8.25rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--indigo);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center;transform:rotate(-12deg);z-index:3;padding:0 .8rem}
.sticker b{display:block;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:1.85rem;line-height:1;margin:.14rem 0 .16rem;color:var(--teal);letter-spacing:-.02em}
.sticker span{display:block;font-size:.56rem;font-weight:700;line-height:1.22}
/* Hero: one label per group (size, name, one-line description), each linking to its group card, and the circle,
   which links to where the groups agree (common format, 19 November 2026). */
.hero .sub{max-width:none}   /* the hero sentence runs the full width of its column */
.hero .cards{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:16px;position:relative;padding:0}
/* each label link sits in its own list item (role="listitem" on the link itself would drop its link role for screen
   readers); the circle is a sibling link after the list, placed against .cards. The labels are white in both modes,
   so their text uses fixed dark colours rather than --muted, which turns pale in dark mode. */
.hero .glabels{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px}
.hero .glabel{display:block;position:relative;text-decoration:none;color:#190d51;background:#fff;border-radius:14px;
  padding:14px 44px 15px 22px;border-left:8px solid var(--gc);box-shadow:0 14px 30px -18px rgba(9,40,54,.55);width:calc(100% - 9.5rem)}
.hero .glabel small{display:block;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.02em;color:#585670;margin-bottom:2px}
.hero .glabel b{display:block;font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700}
.hero .glabel em{display:block;font-style:normal;font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.35;color:#585670;margin-top:3px}
.hero .glabel .chev{position:absolute;right:16px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);font-size:1.15rem;color:#585670}
.hero .glabel:hover b,.hero .glabel:focus-visible b{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
.hero .glabel:focus-visible,.hero .sticker:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--indigo);outline-offset:3px}
.hero .sticker{position:absolute;right:-6px;top:50%;margin:0;width:10.5rem;height:10.5rem;transform:translateY(-50%) rotate(-12deg);
  border:7px solid transparent;text-decoration:none;
  background:linear-gradient(var(--indigo),var(--indigo)) padding-box,conic-gradient(from -78deg,var(--g1) 0 50%,var(--g2) 0 100%) border-box}
.hero .sticker:hover{transform:translateY(-50%) rotate(-12deg) scale(1.03)}
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:53em){
  .hero .glabels{gap:12px}
  .hero .glabel{padding:11px 40px 12px 18px}
  .hero .glabel b{font-size:1.08rem}
  .hero .glabel em{font-size:.84rem}
  .hero .glabel small{font-size:.74rem}
}
@media (max-width:900px){
  .hero .glabel{width:auto}
  .hero .sticker{position:relative;top:auto;right:auto;transform:rotate(-12deg);align-self:center;margin-top:6px}
  .hero .sticker:hover{transform:rotate(-12deg)}
}
/* the map now opens the groups section, so its heading needs no gap above it; the cards follow it */
.head + .sub-head{margin-top:0}
.map-card + .groups-row{margin-top:56px}
@media (min-width:901px){
  .hero-grid{padding-top:clamp(28px,calc(100vh - 41.5rem),80px)}
}
/* Short windows, or large text in a window that isn't tall: a smaller headline and lede keep the buttons
   on the first screen. 46em follows the reader's text size (736px at 16px, 920px at 20px). */
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:46em){
  .hero h1{font-size:min(12.6cqi,8.6vh,5.8rem);margin-bottom:16px}
  .hero .sub{font-size:1.02rem;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:20px}
  .hero .turnout{margin-top:14px}
}
/* very short windows for the text size (under 32em: 512px at the standard text size, 640px at 20px) */
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:32em){
  .hero h1{font-size:min(12.6cqi,7.6vh,5.8rem);margin-bottom:10px}
  .hero .sub{font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.45;margin-bottom:14px}
  .hero .btn{font-size:.98rem}
}
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:43.25em),(min-width:901px) and (max-width:62.5em) and (max-height:53em){
  .hero-grid{align-items:start}
}
/* Narrow, short windows: the hero sentence (with its vote line) and the buttons a little smaller, so the buttons stay on
   the first screen (901x650 and 1024x768 with 20px text, 901x650 at the standard size). Wider windows are unchanged. */
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-width:62.5em) and (max-height:46em){
  .hero .sub{font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.45}
}
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-width:62.5em) and (max-height:32em){
  .hero .sub{font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.4}
  .hero .btn{font-size:.9rem;padding:.6rem 1rem}
}

/* ---------- sections ---------- */
section.block{padding:104px 0}
.head{margin-bottom:46px}
.head h2{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,3.8vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.02em;max-width:22ch;text-wrap:balance}
.head p{font-size:1.12rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:36rem}
.head .head-line{margin-top:18px;max-width:42rem}
.head.side{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.05fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:20px 56px;align-items:end}
.head.side .head-line{margin-top:0}
.deep{background:var(--deep);color:#fff}
.deep h2{color:#fff}
.tint{background:var(--tint)}

/* ---------- group cards: one neutral fill for both, each marked by its colour band and dots ---------- */
.groups-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:28px;margin-top:28px}
.gcard{border-radius:18px;padding:26px 30px 30px;background:var(--gsoft);border-top:12px solid var(--gc)}
.gcard.one{--gc:var(--g1)} .gcard.two{--gc:var(--g2)}
.gtop{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:18px;margin-bottom:20px}
.gtop .big{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:3.7rem;line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.03em;color:var(--heading);white-space:nowrap}
.gtop .big small{font-size:.48em;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0}
.gtop .who{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3;padding-bottom:4px}
.gtop .who b{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;font-size:1.32rem;font-weight:700;font-family:var(--display);letter-spacing:-.01em;line-height:1.15;color:var(--heading)}
.gtop .who b .dot{width:14px;height:14px}
.qbox{background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px 18px;margin-top:12px}
.qbox q{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:1.04rem;line-height:1.45;margin-bottom:12px}
.qbox.lead q{font-size:1.16rem}
.qbox .lab{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:6px}
.pcts{display:flex;gap:8px 20px;font-size:.95rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.pcts span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.pcts b{font-weight:700}
.nn{color:var(--muted);font-weight:400;font-size:.88em}
.small-note{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:22px;max-width:46rem}
.sub-head{margin:84px 0 26px}
.sub-head h3{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,2.6vw,2.4rem);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.015em}

/* ---------- map: one row along the main divide ---------- */
.map-card{position:relative;border:2px solid var(--frame);border-radius:18px;padding:22px 26px 18px;background:var(--card)}
.map-lead{font-weight:600;font-size:1.02rem;margin-bottom:8px;max-width:46rem}
.map-foot{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:8px}
.someone{font:inherit;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.1;background:var(--indigo);color:#fff;border:0;border-radius:6px;padding:.62rem 1rem .64rem;cursor:pointer}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root:not([data-theme="light"]) .someone{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}}
:root[data-theme="dark"] .someone{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}
#map{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;touch-action:manipulation;cursor:crosshair;overflow:visible}
#map .pdot{transition:transform 1.2s cubic-bezier(.2,.75,.2,1),fill .6s ease,opacity .6s ease}
#map .axis{stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2}
#map .axis-label{fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600}
#map .grp-name{fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--text);font-weight:700}
#map .grp-count{fill:var(--muted);font-family:var(--text)}
.map-hint{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px}
.map-hint .h-touch{display:none}
@media (hover:none){.map-hint .h-fine{display:none}.map-hint .h-touch{display:inline}}
.person{position:absolute;z-index:5;width:21rem;background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:14px;padding:16px 18px 14px;box-shadow:0 18px 40px -20px rgba(0,0,0,.5);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.45;pointer-events:none;opacity:0;transform:translateY(4px);transition:opacity .15s ease,transform .15s ease}
.person.on{opacity:1;transform:none}
.person .pg{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-weight:700;font-size:.98rem;margin-bottom:6px}
.person .pn{color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:10px}
.person .pn b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:700}
.person .lean-h{font-weight:600;font-size:.86rem;margin:12px 0 7px}
.lean{display:flex;height:12px;border-radius:99px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--track);gap:2px}
.lean i{display:block;height:100%}
.lean .l1{background:var(--g1)} .lean .l2{background:var(--g2)}
.lean-n{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;font-size:.84rem;margin-top:6px}
.lean-n span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}
.lean-n b{font-weight:700}
.person .note{margin-top:10px;font-size:.86rem;line-height:1.45}
.person .ex{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:9px;margin-top:10px}
.person .ex .exl{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:.84rem;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px}
.person .ex q{display:block}

/* ---------- where they agree: a dark teal ground, not the MP's indigo, so violet never sits on indigo ---------- */
.sea{background:var(--sea);color:#fff}
.sea h2{color:#fff}
.sea .all-list{--g1:#bb8b1a;--g2:#a77be6}
/* ---------- dumbbells ---------- */
.dumb{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:14px;overflow:visible}
.dumb .trk{stroke:var(--trk,var(--track))}
.dumb .rng{stroke:var(--rng,var(--ink))}
.dumb .tick{fill:var(--tk,var(--muted));font-family:var(--text)}
.dumb .ring{stroke:var(--ring,var(--card))}
.vals{display:flex;gap:8px 22px;font-size:.98rem;margin-top:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.vals span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.vals b{font-weight:700}
.nn{color:var(--muted);font-weight:400;font-size:.88em}
/* ---------- pairs ---------- */
.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border-radius:18px;overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:28px;background:var(--card);color:var(--ink)}
.pair .topic{grid-column:1/-1;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:1rem;padding:26px 34px 0}
.pair .topic h3{font-size:1.9rem;line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.015em}
.pair .topic .n{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap}
.half{padding:22px 34px 30px}
.half.split-half{margin:18px 0}
.half.agree{background:var(--agree-bg);color:var(--agree-ink);margin:18px 18px 18px 0;border-radius:14px;--trk:var(--agree-trk);--rng:var(--agree-ink);--tk:var(--agree-ink);--ring:var(--agree-bg)}
.half.agree .nn{color:var(--agree-ink)}
.half q{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:1.14rem;line-height:1.38;min-height:4.14em;margin-top:14px}
.half.agree .pill{background:var(--agree-ink);color:var(--agree-bg)}
details.all{margin-top:8px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3);padding-top:18px}
details.all summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;padding:.2rem 0}
.all-list{list-style:none;margin:16px 0 0;padding:0;column-count:2;column-gap:44px}
.all-list li{break-inside:avoid;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18)}
.all-list q{display:block;font-weight:500;line-height:1.45}
.all-list .vals{color:#d3e6ea;font-size:.9rem;margin-top:4px}
.all-list .nn{color:inherit;opacity:.85}
/* ---------- priorities ---------- */
.how{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:center;background:var(--card);border:2px solid var(--frame);border-radius:14px;padding:26px 32px;margin-bottom:40px}
.costs{display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:flex-end}
.cost{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:.92rem;text-align:center}
.cost b{font-weight:700}
.sq{display:grid;gap:3px}
.sq i{width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--mist);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--teal-dk)}
.sq.s1{grid-template-columns:repeat(1,16px)} .sq.s4{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,16px)} .sq.s9{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,16px)}
.how p.cap{font-size:1.06rem;line-height:1.5;max-width:36rem}
.finding{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;color:var(--heading);font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.3vw,2rem);line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 26px;max-width:44rem;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.prio-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px}
.pcard{background:var(--card);border-radius:14px;padding:26px 26px 24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:2px solid var(--frame)}
@supports (grid-template-rows:subgrid){.pcard{display:grid;grid-row:span 5;grid-template-rows:subgrid;row-gap:0}.pcard .echo{align-self:start}}
.pcard .rank{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:2.6rem;line-height:1;margin-bottom:10px;color:var(--heading)}
.pcard .tt{margin-bottom:22px;flex:1}
.pcard p.t{font-weight:600;font-size:1.06rem;line-height:1.36}
/* each change leads with its net votes, which set the order; one bar on a shared scale (the top change is full width) */
.tally{margin:0 0 12px}
.tally .big{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:.45rem;margin:0 0 12px;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:2.9rem;line-height:.95;color:var(--heading);letter-spacing:-.02em}
.tally .big span{font-family:var(--text);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:0}
.tbar{height:10px;border-radius:5px;background:var(--track);overflow:hidden}
.tbar i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:5px;background:var(--teal)}
.pstats{font-size:.95rem;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.pstats b{font-weight:700}
.pcard .pstats{color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem}
.echo{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:18px;padding-top:14px}
.echo .el{font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px}
.echo .en{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px}
.echo q{display:block;font-size:.93rem;line-height:1.42;margin-bottom:4px}
.echo .vals{font-size:.9rem;margin-top:6px}
.no-card{margin-top:28px;background:var(--indigo);color:#fff;border-radius:18px;padding:34px 38px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:center}
.no-card h3{font-size:2.3rem;line-height:1.05;margin:0 0 14px;color:var(--teal);letter-spacing:-.015em}
.no-card p.t{font-weight:600;font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.36;margin-bottom:14px}
.no-card p.s{color:#cfd2e6;font-size:1rem}
.no-card .tally .big{color:#fff}
.no-card .tally .big span{color:#cfd2e6}
details.rest{margin-top:28px;border-top:2px solid var(--frame);padding-top:18px}
details.rest summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;padding:.2rem 0}
.rest-list{list-style:none;margin:16px 0 0;padding:0}
.rest-list li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem 1fr auto;gap:16px;align-items:baseline;padding:14px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.rest-list .r{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:1.6rem;line-height:1;color:var(--heading)}
.rest-list .t{font-weight:600}
.rest-list .s{font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:.6rem}
.rest-list .rnet{font-family:var(--display);font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--heading)}
.rest-list .rs{font-size:.9rem}
/* ---------- how this worked ---------- */
.steps{list-style:none;margin:0 0 30px;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px}
.step{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;border:2px solid var(--frame);border-radius:14px;padding:24px 24px 26px;background:var(--card)}
.step .fig{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:3rem;line-height:.95;color:var(--heading);letter-spacing:-.02em}
.step h3{font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600;font-size:1.06rem;letter-spacing:0;line-height:1.3;margin-top:4px;color:var(--ink)}
.step p{font-size:.96rem;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted)}
/* ---------- what happens next: the hero's pale teal, with the indigo sticker ---------- */
.next{background:var(--mist);color:var(--indigo);padding:104px 0;position:relative;overflow:hidden}
.next h2{color:var(--indigo);font-size:clamp(2.8rem,5vw,4.6rem);line-height:.98;margin-bottom:24px;letter-spacing:-.025em}
.next-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,38rem) auto;justify-content:start;gap:48px 88px;align-items:center}
.next p{font-size:1.25rem;line-height:1.5;max-width:32rem;margin-bottom:32px}
.next :focus-visible{outline-color:var(--indigo)}
.next .sticker2{justify-self:center;width:15rem;height:15rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--indigo);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center;transform:rotate(-10deg);padding:1.4rem}
.next .sticker2 b{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:2.4rem;line-height:1;display:block;color:var(--teal);letter-spacing:-.02em;max-width:72%;margin:0 auto}
@media (max-width:900px){
  .head.side{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .head.side .head-line{margin-top:18px}
  .pair,.no-card,.next-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .how{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px;padding:22px}
  .costs{gap:20px}
  .steps{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px}
  .step{padding:20px}
  .step .fig{font-size:2.5rem}
  .next{padding:72px 0}
  .next .sticker2{width:10.625rem;height:10.625rem}
  .next .sticker2 b{font-size:1.6rem}
  .half.agree{margin:0 14px 14px}
  .half.split-half{margin:6px 0 0}
  .pair .topic{padding:22px 22px 0;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .pair .topic h3{font-size:1.6rem}
  .half{padding:18px 22px 24px}
  .half q{min-height:0}
  .all-list{column-count:1}
  .prio-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .no-card{padding:28px 22px;gap:22px}
  .rest-list li{grid-template-columns:2.4rem 1fr}
  .rest-list .s{grid-column:2;white-space:normal}
}
@media (max-width:520px){ .steps{grid-template-columns:1fr} }
@media (hover:hover) and (pointer:fine){
  .pair,.pcard,.no-card{transition:opacity .2s ease}
  #pairs:has(.pair:hover) .pair:not(:hover),
  #priorities:has(.pcard:hover) .pcard:not(:hover),
  #priorities:has(.pcard:hover) .no-card,
  #priorities:has(.no-card:hover) .pcard{opacity:.25}
}
@media (hover:hover) and (pointer:fine) and (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ .pair,.pcard,.no-card{transition:none} }

/* ---------- notes (for the full build): every paragraph after a row's heading stays in the right column ---------- */
details.fine{border-top:2px solid var(--frame);padding-top:18px}
details.fine summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;padding:.2rem 0}
details.fine .arows{margin-top:14px}
.arows{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.arow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,2fr);column-gap:32px;padding:24px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.arow > p{grid-column:2}
.arow h3{font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600;font-size:1.08rem;letter-spacing:0;line-height:1.35;color:var(--ink)}
.arow p{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.6;max-width:44rem}
.arow p + p{margin-top:.6rem}

/* ---------- footer ---------- */
footer{background:var(--indigo);color:#fff;padding:48px 0 56px}
.foot{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:32px}
.foot strong{font-weight:700}
.foot .ack{color:#cfd2e6;font-size:.95rem}

@media (max-width:900px){
  .wrap{padding:0 20px}
  .hero-grid,.head,.head.side,.groups-row,.foot,.sub-head{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .head.side .head-line{margin-top:18px}
  .sub-head{margin:64px 0 20px}
  .hero-grid{padding:28px 0 64px;gap:28px}
  .hero h1{font-size:min(12.6cqi,3.9rem)}
  .hero .sub{font-size:1.08rem}
  .cards{gap:16px;padding:6px 4px 10px}
  .sticker{position:relative;top:auto;right:auto;align-self:center;margin-top:8px}
  section.block{padding:72px 0}
  .head{gap:18px;margin-bottom:30px}
  .gtop .big{font-size:3rem}
  .gcard{padding:22px 20px 24px}
  .map-card{padding:16px 14px 14px;border-radius:14px}
  .person{position:static;width:auto;opacity:1;transform:none;margin-top:12px;box-shadow:none;display:none}
  .person.on{display:block}
  .arow{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:6px;padding:18px 0}
  .arow > p{grid-column:auto}
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ #map .pdot,.person,.gl{transition:none} .btn:hover,.gl:hover{transform:none} }

/* ---------- RxC site shell (shared with the other project microsites) ---------- */
.rxc-shell{--ink:#17203A;--paper:#fff;--common:#EDFF38;--quiet:#5F657E;--hair:#D9DBE3;--voice-b:#E23A6B;
  font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;box-sizing:border-box}
.rxc-shell *{box-sizing:border-box;font-family:inherit;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit}
.rxc-shell a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}
.rxc-shell a:hover{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.3em}
.rxc-shell a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #2B3EFF;outline-offset:3px}
.rxc-shell .wrap{max-width:78rem;margin:0 auto;padding:.75rem clamp(1.25rem,4vw,4.5rem);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.rxc-shell.top{border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink)}
.rxc-shell.bottom{border-top:1px solid var(--hair);font-size:14px;color:var(--quiet)}
.rxc-shell.bottom a{color:var(--ink)}
.rxc-shell .crumbs{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;color:var(--quiet);min-width:0}
.rxc-shell .crumbs a{font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem}
.rxc-shell .crumbs span.here{overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}
.rxc-shell .status{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;color:var(--quiet)}
.rxc-shell .status i{width:.5rem;height:.5rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--voice-b);display:inline-block}
.rxc-shell .btn{border:2px solid var(--ink);padding:.45rem .8rem;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;line-height:1;color:var(--ink);font-family:inherit;letter-spacing:0}
.rxc-shell .btn:hover{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);text-decoration:none}
.rxc-shell .right{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.rxc-shell .btn{border-radius:0;background:transparent;display:inline-block}
.rxc-shell .btn:hover{transform:none}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="rxc-shell top" role="banner">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="12" height="12"/><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12"/></svg>RadicalxChange</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/projects/">Projects</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="here">Kooyong on migration</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="right">
      <span class="status"><i></i><span data-k="status">Preliminary results, data to 5:08am AEDT, 19 November 2026</span></span>
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:info@radicalxchange.org?subject=Kooyong%20migration%20results">Contact the team</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<header class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1><span class="ln">Kooyong wants</span><span class="ln"><span class="box">a bipartisan plan</span></span><span class="ln">for migration</span></h1>
        <p class="sub" data-k="herosub">People disagree about how many should come, and who should come first. But most in both groups want a bipartisan migration plan that looks at least 10 years ahead. When people voted on priorities, planning migration with housing and infrastructure came first.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn solid" href="#groups">See what Kooyong said</a><a class="btn line" href="#priorities">The changes people want most</a></div>
        <p class="turnout" data-k="turnout">Since 9 November 2026 · 102 people have taken part · 89 in a group</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="glabels" role="list" aria-label="The two groups">
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-1" style="--gc:var(--g1)"><small data-k="hl1n">Group 1 · 61 people</small><b data-k="hl1name">Migration works</b><em data-k="hl1desc">Migration keeps us going; tackle problems without blaming it.</em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-2" style="--gc:var(--g2)"><small data-k="hl2n">Group 2 · 28 people</small><b data-k="hl2name">Fewer, but flexible</b><em data-k="hl2desc">Too many, too quickly; put people who can work first.</em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
        </div>
        <a class="sticker" href="#agree" aria-label="More than 4 in 5 in both groups want a bipartisan migration plan, 10 or more years ahead. See what they agree on."><div aria-hidden="true"><span>More than</span><b data-k="sticker">4 in 5</b><span>in both groups want a bipartisan migration plan, 10 or more years ahead</span></div></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
<section class="block" id="groups" aria-labelledby="groups-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="groups-h">Most people fit into one of two groups</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="sub-head"><h3>Where everyone sits</h3></div>
    <div class="map-card" id="map-card">
      <p class="map-lead">Each dot is one person, placed by how they voted. People who voted alike sit close together, so the higher the pile, the more people voted that way.</p>
      <svg id="map" role="img" aria-label="A map of everyone placed in a group, along the main divide: Group 1 on the left, Group 2 on the right."></svg>
      <div class="map-foot">
        <button class="someone" type="button" id="someone">Show me someone</button>
      </div>
      <div class="person" id="person" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <p class="map-hint"><span class="h-fine">Hover over a dot to see how that person voted.</span><span class="h-touch">Tap the map or press “Show me someone” to see how one person voted.</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="groups-row">
      <div class="gcard one" id="group-1">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big" data-k="g1f">2<small> in </small>3</span><span class="who"><b data-k="gc1name"><i class="dot g1"></i>Group 1: Migration works</b><span data-k="g1n">61 people</span></span></div>
        <div class="qbox lead"><p class="lab">What sets them apart</p><q data-k="t:8">Migration keeps my workplace and my community going. Cutting it back would cost us more than it would save.</q>
          <div class="pcts" data-k="c1:8"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>90%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>30%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q data-k="t:92">Concerns around economy, infrastructure, etc are valid - but should be addressed as separate policy issues rather than blaming migration</q>
          <div class="pcts" data-k="c1:92"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>98%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>28%</b> of Group 2 <span class="nn">(18 voted)</span></span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q data-k="t:34">As a lucky country, we have a duty to keep helping people who aren't so lucky, even when it costs us.</q>
          <div class="pcts" data-k="c1:34"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>91%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>19%</b> of Group 2</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="gcard two" id="group-2">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big" data-k="g2f">1<small> in </small>3</span><span class="who"><b data-k="gc2name"><i class="dot g2"></i>Group 2: Fewer, but flexible</b><span data-k="g2n">28 people</span></span></div>
        <div class="qbox lead"><p class="lab">What sets them apart</p><q data-k="t:3">For me, trust comes down to the numbers: too many people have arrived too quickly for our communities to keep up.</q>
          <div class="pcts" data-k="c2:3"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>74%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>21%</b> of Group 1</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q data-k="t:21">When places are limited, people who can work and contribute economically should take priority over family reunion.</q>
          <div class="pcts" data-k="c2:21"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>85%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>19%</b> of Group 1</span></div></div>
        <div class="qbox"><q data-k="t:52">The migration program needs to ensure the people we accept are suitable and genuinely wanting to embrace our culture and way of life.</q>
          <div class="pcts" data-k="c2:52"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>100%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>37%</b> of Group 1</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small-note" data-k="caveat">The people who joined in aren’t a random sample, so these groups describe who took part, not all of Kooyong. 13 people aren’t in a group: they voted on too few statements, or didn’t agree or disagree with any.</p>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="block sea" id="agree" aria-labelledby="agree-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head side">
      <h2 id="agree-h">Even where they disagree, they agree on something</h2>
      <p class="head-line" data-k="agreelead">At least 7 in 10 people in each group agreed with 21 statements. Here are five of them, each beside a related statement the two groups disagree on.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="pairs"></div>
    <details class="all">
      <summary data-k="foldsum">See all 21 statements both groups agreed with</summary>
      <ol class="all-list" id="all"></ol>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block tint" id="priorities" aria-labelledby="prio-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="prio-h">The six changes people want most</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="how">
      <div class="costs" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s1"><i></i></div><p><b>1 vote</b><br>1 credit</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s4"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>2 votes</b><br>4 credits</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s9"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>3 votes</b><br>9 credits</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="cap" data-k="qvcap">At a community session on 9 November, 52 people used quadratic voting to spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, for or against. Each extra vote on the same idea costs more, so the totals show what people care about most.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="finding" data-k="finding">Three of the top six match ideas most people in both groups agreed with in the conversation.</p>
    <div class="prio-grid" id="prio"></div>
    <div class="no-card">
      <div><h3>And one clear no</h3><p class="t" data-k="no-t">Prioritise migrants in high-paying jobs, using salary rather than shortage lists to decide who qualifies.</p><p class="s" data-k="no-s">32 people opposed it and 8 backed it.</p></div>
      <div><div class="tally"><p class="big" data-k="no-net">−49<span>net votes</span></p></div></div>
    </div>
    <details class="rest">
      <summary>See the other six changes</summary>
      <ol class="rest-list" id="rest"></ol>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2 id="about-h">How this worked</h2></div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step"><span class="fig" data-k="st-starters">36</span><h3>Starter statements</h3><p data-k="st-starters-p">The conversation opened with 36 statements for people to agree or disagree with.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig" data-k="st-people">102</span><h3>People took part</h3><p data-k="st-people-p">Since 9 November they have voted agree, disagree or pass, and added statements of their own.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">2</span><h3>Groups emerged</h3><p>Polis, an open-source tool, grouped people who voted alike. Nobody chose a group. We named them.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig" data-k="st-voters">52</span><h3>Voters set priorities</h3><p data-k="st-voters-p">On 9 November they spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, using quadratic voting.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <details class="fine">
      <summary>Notes for checking the numbers</summary>
      <div class="arows">
        <div class="arow"><h3>Reading the percentages</h3><p>Each figure is the share of a group who agreed, out of those in the group who voted on that statement. Later statements had fewer voters, so where fewer than 20 people in a group voted, we show how many.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Reading the map</h3><p>We rebuilt the map from the published votes using the same method as Polis, so people sit close to where the Polis report places them, but not in exactly the same spots. Left to right is the main divide in the votes. Where many people sit close together, their dots pile up, so a dot can sit a little to one side of its exact place.</p><p>Each person’s card shows up to two of their votes as examples. For each group they sided with, it shows the statement most of that group agreed with, preferring statements the person agreed with over ones they rejected.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Inside the groups</h3><p data-k="n-inside">We also looked for a clear split inside each group. Neither has one that holds up. In Group 1, the clearest split rests on only four statements, two of them saying the same thing, with fewer than 25 voters on one side. Group 2 is too small to test.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Unlikely allies</h3><p data-k="n-allies">We also looked for unlikely allies, people in both groups who back the same statements, and found none that held up.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The group cards</h3><p>Each card shows three statements most of the group agreed with and far fewer of the other group did. RadicalxChange chose which three to show. We chose statements about what each group wants, including what it values. Lines that mainly judge other people count in every figure, but aren’t on the cards.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Who and what we counted</h3><p data-k="n-stmts">169 statements were open for voting: the 36 starter statements and 133 written by people taking part. The moderators held back 14 others, and 2 more were still waiting for review, so no one else voted on them.</p><p data-k="n-people">We count the 102 people who voted on at least one of those 169 statements, the same as Polis’s own count. Between them they cast 9,992 votes.</p><p data-k="n-pass">One person voted on enough statements to be placed in a group, but didn’t agree or disagree with any of them: every vote they cast was a pass. They count as taking part, but we haven’t placed them in a group, because a pass doesn’t show where someone stands. Polis places them anyway, because it reads a pass as halfway between agree and disagree.</p><p data-k="n-own">One other person’s only vote was the agreement Polis records when someone adds a statement. They count as taking part, but voted on too few statements to be placed in a group.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Pairing the statements</h3><p>RadicalxChange chose which statements to pair. Every number comes straight from the results.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The priority vote</h3><p data-k="n-qv">A separate vote with its own voters. We set aside ballots that used fewer than 10 credits (there was one, and it was empty). Where someone voted more than once, we counted the last ballot they submitted. That leaves 52 voters. Net votes are votes for minus votes against. The matching statements from the conversation are close in meaning, not identical in wording.</p><p data-k="n-chart">The chart shared after the session shows 54 voters. It counts names that differ only in capital letters or spacing as different people, and where one person sent two ballots that used the same credits, it kept the first rather than the last. The top six are the same, in the same order.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The data</h3><p data-k="n-data">From the Polis export of 19 November 2026, 5:08am AEDT. The conversation is still open, so these results are preliminary. Statements appear exactly as people wrote them.</p></div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

